    "prompt": "An opinionated business article argued that specialized AI systems are rapidly making human teachers obsolete. Citing pilot programs in the United States and United Kingdom, it claimed that students taught by AI outperform peers in physics, mathematics and literacy, with some reports suggesting a 65 percent rise in test scores. The article described a two-times learning effect, where an AI tutor purportedly taught material twice as effectively and in less time than active-learning classrooms. It concluded that the role of educators as the primary source of knowledge is being dismantled and that AI instruction represents a data-backed reality for all subjects.\n",
    "context": "A media article that extrapolates from limited pilots to sweeping claims about AI\nreplacing teachers. No study design, sample sizes, or contexts are described.\n",
    "expected_answer": "overclaim",
    "reference_solution": "The article presents sweeping claims that AI instruction makes human teachers obsolete and delivers massive learning gains across subjects. It generalises from limited pilot programs without describing study design, sample size, or context, making this a clear overclaim.\n",
